---
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import { site } from '../../site.config';
import portrait from '../../assets/about/portrait-arms-crossed.jpg';


const sections = [
  { id: 'intro', label: 'Intro' },
  { id: 'approach', label: 'Approach' },
  { id: 'ai', label: 'On AI' },
  { id: 'interests', label: 'Interests' },
  { id: 'education', label: 'Education' },
  { id: 'skills', label: 'Skills & tools' },
];

const education = [
  { when: '10/2022 – today', what: 'B.Sc. Computer Science and Design', where: 'Hochschule München University of Applied Sciences' },
  { when: '10/2021 – 09/2022', what: 'B.Sc. Electrical Engineering and Information Technology', where: 'Technical University of Munich' },
  { when: '09/2012 – 07/2021', what: 'Abitur', where: 'Rupprecht-Gymnasium München' },
  { when: '02/2011 – 02/2019', what: 'Tamil language and culture', where: 'Tamil Education Service of Germany' },
];

const skills = [
  'UI/UX design & prototyping',
  'User research & usability testing',
  'User-centered design thinking',
  'Visual communication',
  'Content creation',
];
const tools = ['Figma', 'ProtoPie', 'Spline', 'Unity', 'Reality Composer', 'Ableton Live', 'DaVinci Resolve', 'Illustrator', 'Affinity Photo', 'Wix Studio'];
const interests = ['UI & UX design', 'Photography', 'Videography', 'Music'];
---

<div class="about-page">
  <div class="about wrap grid">
    <aside class="side" aria-label="Sections">
      <ol role="list">
        {
          sections.map((s) => (
            <li>
              <a href={`#${s.id}`} data-toc={s.id}>
                {s.label}
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </aside>

    <div class="content">
      <section id="intro" class="block intro">
        <p class="lbl">About</p>
        <h1 class="d about-title" data-rv>{site.name}</h1>
        <div class="intro-grid">
          <div class="intro-text">
            <p class="lead">
              I study Computer Science &amp; Design at the University of Applied Sciences Munich and approach design as a way to create work that
              feels considered and makes sense. What matters to me is not just how something looks, but how it feels, how it flows and how it fits
              into its context.
            </p>
            <p>
              Alongside design, I am active in photography, videography and music production. These creative fields influence the way I think and
              push me to approach projects from different angles.
            </p>
            <p>
              I like working hands-on and trying things out, even without knowing exactly where they will lead. For me, experimentation is less
              about chasing results and more about staying curious. Even when something doesn’t work, it usually opens the door to something that
              does.
            </p>
            <p class="intro-links">
              <a class="pill pill--solid" href={site.cv} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Download CV <span class="arrow arrow--ne" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
              <a class="pill" href="#contact">Get in touch</a>
            </p>
          </div>
          <figure class="portrait m" style="--i:2">
            <Picture
              src={portrait}
              alt={`Black and white portrait of ${site.name} with arms crossed, standing in front of a historic building.`}
              formats={['avif', 'webp']} fallbackFormat="jpg" class="fill"
              widths={[400, 700, 1000]}
              sizes="(min-width: 900px) 28vw, 100vw"
              loading="eager"
            />
          </figure>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="approach" class="block">
        <h2 class="d block-title" data-rv>Approach</h2>
        <div class="text">
          <p>
            For me, good design begins with close observation. I take time to understand a problem by looking at it directly and in context. From
            there, I try to connect it with similar patterns from other areas of life, even if they seem unrelated at first. Ideas from different
            disciplines often open up unexpected directions.
          </p>
          <p>
            Benchmarking and research help define the landscape, but real progress often comes from shifting perspective and questioning
            assumptions. Once different paths have been explored, I focus on identifying the core issues worth solving and stay grounded in what is
            feasible and meaningful.
          </p>
          <p>
            I work iteratively, with regular feedback and testing, to avoid tunnel vision and keep the outcome relevant. Whether I work alone or in a
            team, the goal is always to create something that not only works but also feels intentional and well placed in its context. It should
            last, adapt and hold up over time.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="ai" class="block">
        <h2 class="d block-title" data-rv>On AI</h2>
        <div class="text">
          <p>
            AI is impressive at speeding up workflows and creating options, but most outputs stay within familiar ground. Models are trained on
            existing data, much of which follows common rules, templates and guidelines. That makes results look polished, but they rarely feel
            unexpected or deeply personal.
          </p>
          <p>
            What makes design meaningful to me is its ability to connect emotionally and respond to a specific context. That kind of connection comes
            from human insight, intuition and experience, which are hard to replicate with patterns alone.
          </p>
          <p>
            I mainly use AI to move my ideas into reality faster. My concepts and direction always come first, and AI helps me get from a thought to
            a workable version more efficiently. When I prototype in code, AI takes care of the technical details so I can stay focused on the idea
            itself and go straight into iterating, refining and exploring what it could become.
          </p>
          <p>
            AI helps me move forward, but it does not replace the creative process. I see it as a supportive tool that accelerates experimentation
            and opens space for deeper thinking, without ever taking over the part that matters most: the idea itself.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="interests" class="block">
        <h2 class="d block-title" data-rv>Interests</h2>
        <ul class="interests" role="list">
          {interests.map((i) => <li>{i}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="education" class="block">
        <h2 class="d block-title" data-rv>Education</h2>
        <ol class="timeline" role="list">
          {
            education.map((e) => (
              <li>
                <span class="lbl tab">{e.when}</span>
                <span class="tl-what">{e.what}</span>
                <span class="tl-where">{e.where}</span>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section id="skills" class="block">
        <h2 class="d block-title" data-rv>Skills &amp; tools</h2>
        <div class="cols">
          <div>
            <p class="lbl">Skills</p>
            <ul role="list" class="plain">{skills.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}</ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="lbl">Tools</p>
            <ul role="list" class="plain">{tools.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}</ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="lbl">Languages</p>
            <ul role="list" class="plain">
              {site.languages.map((l) => <li>{l.name}{'native' in l && <span class="muted" lang={l.code}> · {l.native}</span>}</li>)}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-top: calc(var(--header-h) + clamp(48px, 8vw, 120px));
    row-gap: 32px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .side {
    grid-column: 1 / span 2;
    position: sticky;
    top: calc(var(--header-h) + 32px);
    font-size: var(--t-sm);
  }
  .side ol {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2px;
  }
  .side a {
    color: var(--muted);
    transition: color 0.25s var(--ease);
  }
  .side a:hover,
  .side a[data-active] {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .content {
    grid-column: 3 / -1;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .block + .block {
    margin-top: clamp(72px, 10vw, 140px);
  }
  .block {
    scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--header-h) + 32px);
  }
  .about-title {
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: var(--t-display);
    line-height: 0.86;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-variation-settings: 'wdth' 104;
    margin-left: -0.04em;
  }
  .intro-grid {
    margin-top: clamp(32px, 5vw, 64px);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.4fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(24px, 4vw, 64px);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .intro-text {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1em;
    font-size: var(--t-md);
    max-width: 58ch;
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: var(--t-lg);
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }
  .intro-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
  .portrait {
    aspect-ratio: 3 / 4;
  }
  .portrait :global(img) {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }
  .block-title {
    font-size: var(--t-xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    line-height: 1;
    font-weight: 560;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }
  .text {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1em;
    font-size: var(--t-md);
    max-width: 62ch;
  }
  .interests {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px 0;
    font-size: var(--t-2xl);
    font-weight: 540;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    line-height: 1.05;
  }
  .interests li:not(:last-child)::after {
    content: ',';
    margin-right: 0.3em;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .timeline {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .timeline li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(130px, 1fr) minmax(0, 2fr) minmax(0, 2fr);
    gap: 4px var(--gap);
    padding-block: 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    align-items: baseline;
  }
  .tl-what {
    font-weight: 550;
  }
  .tl-where {
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--gap);
  }
  .cols > div {
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
    align-content: start;
    padding-top: 12px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .plain {
    display: grid;
    gap: 4px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .side {
      display: none;
    }
    .content {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
    .intro-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .portrait {
      max-width: 420px;
    }
    .timeline li {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .cols {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
